text:
\emph{$\alpha$-conversion} ($\aconv$) is inductively defined as follows:
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item If $P \aconv Q$ and $Q \aconv R$, then $P \aconv R$.
    \ollabel{defn:aconv1}
  \item If $P \aconvone Q$, then $P \aconv Q$. \ollabel{defn:aconv2}
  \item $P \aconv P$. \ollabel{defn:aconv3}
  \end{enumerate}
